---
description: dbt SQL model style
globs:
  - "models/**/*.sql"
---

Use dbt SQL best practices.

- Use `source()` only in staging/source-shaped models.
- Use `ref()` for dbt model dependencies in intermediate and marts models.
- Avoid `SELECT *` in marts.
- Use clear column aliases.
- Keep staging logic simple and source-shaped.
- Keep reusable business logic in intermediate models.
- Keep final reporting logic in marts.
- Do not duplicate metric formulas across many models.
- Add comments only when they explain business logic or non-obvious technical choices.
